https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/vkd3d (the Wine project). Direct3D 12 on
Vulkan: the native Linux game draws through it. The download carries
libvkd3d.so.1, libvkd3d-shader.so.1 and libvkd3d-utils.so.1 in linux/lib (the
builder copies them to <install>/lib), built UNMODIFIED from the official
vkd3d 2.1 release tarball with zig cc for glibc 2.31 by the build script
packaging/linux/build_vkd3d_zig.sh. The game loads them at run time with
dlopen (it does not link them), so a player can replace them with any
interface-compatible build, e.g. their distribution's. The complete
corresponding source -- the release tarball itself, vkd3d-2.1.tar.xz (SHA-256
7510146aff2adfb4ae07ab890701a607e5ff7c66e57100cfc9f630ec92eeda6a), and the
build script -- ships in the download in linux/lib/source and is copied with
the libraries to <install>/lib/source. vkd3d's own notices follow, as the
release has them: COPYING, AUTHORS and LICENSE (the full LGPL-2.1).
vkd3d-shader includes a SPIR-V grammar table generated from the Khronos SPIR-V
grammar and two parsers generated by GNU Bison (under Bison's special
exception); their notices close this section.

