================================================================================
4. Linked into the game from the zig toolchain
================================================================================

The builder compiles and links the game with zig 0.16.0 (clang): target
x86_64-linux-gnu.2.31 for the native build, x86_64-windows-gnu for the Proton
build. The builder fetches the pinned zig-x86_64-linux-0.16.0 from ziglang.org
and checks its SHA-256 before use; the offline flavor of the download carries
that same official tarball unmodified in toolchain/, with zig's own license
files inside it (zig is MIT; the LLVM, clang and lld code built into the zig
program is Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception). The produced game and the Project
8 Plus plugins the download carries (thp8_mod_p8plus.so for native,
thp8_mod_p8plus.dll for Proton, built with the same pinned zig) statically
link parts of zig's distribution, listed below. The native game links the
system's glibc, libm, libdl, librt and libpthread dynamically; they are part
of the player's Linux system and are not distributed.

